' Source: apps/api-node/src/modules/posts/application/post.use-cases.ts
' Main entity migration: apps/api-node/src/migrations/002_lost_found_schema.sql
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "User" as Actor
participant "My Posts Page" as Page
participant "Posts API" as API
participant "Post Service" as Service
participant "posts" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open View my posts
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: GET /api/posts/mine
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: View my posts
activate Service
Service -> Table: 5: SELECT own posts with allowed filters and paging
activate Table
Table --> Service: 6: Own posts and total
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 7: Add viewer-scoped matching summaries and protected media URLs
Service --> API: 8: Own post cards
API --> Page: 9: HTTP 200: Own post cards
Page --> Actor: 10: Show authorized result
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 / 401 / 403 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Related tables, authorization, transactions and audit remain inside the service. Catalogue status is
not deployment or manual acceptance.
endlegend
@enduml
